information-acts-and-common-ground-lines-2 = cons "Avik Jain" (cons "" (cons "Interaction in hyperactivity is continuous real-time coupling over shared common ground rather than discrete turn-based messaging. Every screen or channel presents structured information together with the exact capacity for action warranted by what is observed — never leaking internal compiler vocabulary into human interaction." (cons "" (cons "Hyperactivity is a technological work determined directly by the empirical science of human happiness (developed out of study with Dacher Keltner at UC Berkeley). Human flourishing is not an external rubric or post-hoc evaluation score applied to judge the system from outside: there are no external assessment criteria, because the system's continuation is deterministic and its properties follow by mathematical necessity across human cognition, neuroscience, and computation." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "Putting programs, specifications, and proofs " (cons "in one language" (cons " is only the elementary precondition — natural English was already one language in which rational minds could carry out exact inference. The substantive contribution is characterizing what is amenable to rule-based computational reasoning across an entire information space. In hyperactivity, the entire technological operation of a trading and research institution such as Citadel Securities — execution fleet, quantitative research infrastructure, hardware targets, and institutional knowledge — becomes a single program supporting end-to-end machine verification and computational reasoning over every provable property of the whole." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "Accordingly, hyperactivity is not a single domain-specific empirical investigation into nature; it is a fundamental formal exposition of relational reality that enables arbitrary concrete and abstract research across every domain." nil))))))))
